WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.373
Evaluating the diversity of face datasets almost
always relies on categorical demographic labels such as race,

00:00:04.453 --> 00:00:08.827
gender, or age.

00:00:08.907 --> 00:00:13.280
But these labels are frequently unavailable,
legally restricted to collect,

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:17.733
and prone to bias when they are inferred by
annotators rather than self-reported.

00:00:17.813 --> 00:00:22.187
Worse,

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:26.640
categorical labels flatten the continuous nature of
human appearance: skin tone becomes simply light or dark,

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:31.093
and two faces sharing the same label can still look
strikingly different.

00:00:31.173 --> 00:00:35.547
Rigid taxonomies also erase multi-ethnic people,
shift meaning across cultures,

00:00:35.627 --> 00:00:40.000
and can cause real psychological harm when someone
is mislabeled.
